# Calculators and Internal Links

Use this rule when adding calculator references, methodology links, related reading, or internal links.

## Do

- Link only to live articles, calculators, methodology pages, tools, or data pages that exist in the repo.
- Verify the target path before adding or changing an internal link.
- Use descriptive anchor text that tells the reader what the linked page does.
- Link to calculator methodology or inspect-the-arithmetic pages when the article relies on a calculator's assumptions.
- Keep related links relevant to the reader's current calculation or decision.
- Preserve existing valid internal links unless the linked page has moved.
- When a live calculator and an article answer the same reader question, add both shared call-outs (`calculatorCallout` on the article, `CALCULATOR_PRIMARY_ARTICLE` on the calculator). See `75-article-calculator-callout.mdc`.

## Do Not

- Do not add placeholder links, future links, empty anchors, or guessed slugs.
- Do not link to drafts from production pages unless the user explicitly requests it.
- Do not use vague anchors such as "click here", "learn more", or "this article" when a specific anchor is possible.
- Do not imply a calculator supports an assumption, tax year, province, or formula it does not actually support.
